Fundamental terms and definitions in energy economics;
Supply of fossil fuels and their role in global warming as well as supply and ramp up of renewable energies usage.
Technical, energetic and economic description and balancing of energy usage ranging from energy services to primary energy (including renewable energies);
Energy markets, instruments for modelling and analysis of energy equipment and systems;
Concepts of energy transition towards a sustainable future energy system including the role of hydrogen

OBJECTIVES:
At the end of the module, students are able to:
- understand the principles of energy supply and the properties of provision of applied energy carriers,
- provide an overview of the generation of electrical energy and the properties of the applied power plants,
- analyse and assess the operating method of power plants based on requirements arising from fulfilments of energy demand and sustainable development schemes
