CONTENT:
The Seminar "Multirate Signal Processing" focuses mainly on interpolation/decimation theory and polyphase filter architectures which are essential for designing efficient signal processing structures in communication systems also including asynchronous sampling rate conversion and fundamentals of digital signal synthesis. The lectures are subdivided into the follwing parts:
1 Applications of Multirate Signal Processing - Audio and Videosignal Processing, Mobile Communications;2 Principles of Sampling Rate Conversion - Polyphase and Modulation Representation;
3 Interpolation/Decimation Filters - Characteristics and Design;
4 Digital Signal Synthesis - What is DDS?, Applications; 
5 Bandpass Sub-Sampling - Sampling Theorem for Bandpass Signals, Applications; 
6 Asynchronous Sampling Rate Conversion - Problem Description and Functional Principle;
The theory fundamentals are explained by practical examples and exercises. A detailed script comprises all presented topics.

OBJECTIVES:
Students shall learn in this module to design and dimension sampling rate converters, to understand the theory and background and to employ various implementation forms. Furthermore, at the end of the term students shall be able to combine sampling rate converts with other signal processing techniques, e.g. band-pass sub-sampling, and also to understand the economical aspects of different implementations.

